WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.884
Welcome to the class of 2022.

00:00:03.884 --> 00:00:07.181
To start our online kickoff,
I thought I'd take you outside for

00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:10.900
a quick tour of some of my
favorite places at Stanford.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.520
Let's start at Coupa.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.330
You'll quickly discover that
there are several Coupa cafes on

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.800
the Stanford campus.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.580
The GSB one is the best.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.399
It's the center of activity on campus and
Dean Lowery's unofficial office.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.310
Last week,
I was trying to keep a low profile.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.395
But I had a chance meeting with a few
earlier rivals from your class.

00:00:30.395 --> 00:00:32.579
That made my day.

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:36.100
[MUSIC]

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.368
Town Square is the heart of the GSB,
the tents and

00:00:39.368 --> 00:00:42.336
the outer furniture are recent additions.

00:00:42.336 --> 00:00:46.841
Phil Knights footsteps are a reminder
of the people who've come before you

00:00:46.841 --> 00:00:50.100
at the GSB and whose shoes you're filling.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.840
When the Knight Management Center
was built,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.785
the artists Peter Wagner
design the cornerstone.

00:00:55.785 --> 00:01:00.350
He perfectly captured the GSB,
dedicated to

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.770
the things that haven't happened yet and
the people who are about to dream them up.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.353
I first came to Stanford as
an undergraduate in 1990 and

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:13.047
joined the faculty ten years later.

00:01:13.047 --> 00:01:15.425
I'm still amazed by
the beauty of the campus.

00:01:16.705 --> 00:01:21.575
The Rodin Sculpture Garden is one of
the famous places on the Stanford campus.

00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:22.865
And for those of you with children,

00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:26.425
it's one of the few museums
that our kids actually enjoy.

00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:31.087
Some people think the Coupa Cafe in your
Green library is as good as the one at

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:32.426
the GSB mistakenly.

00:01:32.426 --> 00:01:35.929
[MUSIC]

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:40.038
I hope you all will make an effort to
experience Stanford beyond the GSB and

00:01:40.038 --> 00:01:44.410
to meet the brilliant students and
faculty in Law, Medicine, Engineering,

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.980
Education, Sustainability and
other fields.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.210
I promise it will inspire you.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.199
Of course, the physical campus is one
part of what makes Stanford special, but

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:57.630
it's not the important part.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.990
It's the people you will meet and

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:03.190
the relationships you'll form that will
truly make your time here memorable.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.620
So again, welcome to the GSB.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.253
We can't wait to see what you dream up.

